# The launchers and manifests must reach every client byte-for-byte. A Windows
# git client with core.autocrlf=true (the Git for Windows default) would
# otherwise check run-hook.sh out with CRLF endings, which sh rejects at the
# first `then`, and rewrite hooks.json, which Codex hashes for plugin trust.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.ps1   text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
